25
00:01:22,200 --> 00:01:26,520
It works out at roughly one
sale for every 5,900 letters.

26
00:01:26,520 --> 00:01:29,840
Think of it like knocking on
200 doors to get one to open.

27
00:01:29,840 --> 00:01:33,350
Most owners aren't thinking about
selling when the letter lands.

28
00:01:33,440 --> 00:01:36,250
Some keep it in a drawer for a
year, then something changes.

29
00:01:36,400 --> 00:01:40,190
A tenant leaves, a loan comes up
for renewal, a partner wants out.

30
00:01:40,210 --> 00:01:41,320
And that's when they call.

31
00:01:41,320 --> 00:01:44,470
That's why we write to the
same owner every three months.

32
00:01:44,470 --> 00:01:46,720
The letter isn't meant to persuade anyone.

33
00:01:46,720 --> 00:01:49,200
